 "description": "The COMPENSATED self/world/board discriminator: a region is controllable only if my action predicts its motion better than its own inertia (action-conditioned surprise < passive surprise, by a margin). The agent compensates for each object's own dynamics; robust to autonomous objects that change their own velocity, with no randomising or threshold-tuning from outside. Generated by scripts/gen_action_corr_seed.py.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "nd_action_correlation",
  "description": "self = my action beats inertia at predicting it; world = inertia/own-dynamics predicts it (or nothing does); board = still."
 },
